      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #43145.\n\nFor Inkling, `apply_reasoning_enabled(request, False)` sets `reasoning_effort=\"none\"`, but `_get_reasoning_from_request` falls back to the detector's always-on default. The request therefore still requires reasoning in the grammar and response parsing paths. The read-side decision should agree with the effort used to encode the messages.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add an Inkling branch to the shared reasoning decision, reusing `_parse_inkling_reasoning_effort` and the cached server default. Zero effort disables reasoning; positive effort enables it. Explicit server-level `force_reasoning` behavior is preserved.\n- Extend the existing Inkling tests to check disable/read-back and a table of explicit, positive, and default efforts. Use `CustomTestCase` for the touched registered test class.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nThe branch includes upstream main 51faf523 and the CI-required base b6778515.\nThe combined OpenAI/Anthropic serving suites passed **225 tests with 132 subtests**\non the tested merge commit 74926c0a. The regression fails before the fix.\n\nValidation uses Python 3.12.13, Torch 2.14.1+cu130, sglang-kernel 0.4.10,\nFlashInfer 0.7.2 and Transformers 5.19.0. The request fixtures run on CPU in the\nCUDA-enabled pinned runtime and import the actual source modules.\nModel inference/accuracy and full upstream serving CI remain unverified;\nupstream serving tests require maintainer authorization through run-ci.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo performance benchmark was run. This is a serving decision fix; no kernel or scheduling code changes.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Run the full configured pre-commit hooks on both changed files: passed, including registration checks and git diff --check.\n- [x] Add focused unit tests using the registered CPU test conventions.\n- [x] Assess documentation needs: no public API or configuration changes.\n- [ ] Complete applicable model validation and upstream CI. GPU/model checks remain pending; no speed claim is made.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\nImplementation and regression tests were prepared with Codex assistance. Human review and maintainer approvals remain pending.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38869056225](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38869056225)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38869056275](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38869056275)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38869056254](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38869056254)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
